From: bs <bs@asusrt-ac1200g-plus>
Date: Wed, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: bgmac: use 64-byte TX DMA bursts on BCM53573

BCM53573 has a hardware erratum (BCM53573 erratum #bgmac-tx128): when the
GMAC core's rev 8 BGMAC_FEAT_TX_MASK_SETUP is present, 128-byte TX bursts
corrupt 0.1-4 % of frames under heavy forwarding (400-900 Mbit/s). Fix
by selecting 64-byte bursts (BGMAC_DMA_TX_BL_64) instead of the default
128-byte value.

Cf. third_party/archer-c1200-v2-openwrt/openwrt/patches-6.12/323-*.

Signed-off-by: bs <bs@asusrt-ac1200g-plus>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/bgmac.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/bgmac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/bgmac.c
@@ -92,7 +92,9 @@ static void bgmac_dma_tx_enable(struct bg
 	ctl = bgmac_read(bgmac, ring->mmio_base + BGMAC_DMA_TX_CTL);
 	if (bgmac->feature_flags & BGMAC_FEAT_TX_MASK_SETUP) {
 		ctl &= ~BGMAC_DMA_TX_BL_MASK;
-		ctl |= BGMAC_DMA_TX_BL_128 << BGMAC_DMA_TX_BL_SHIFT;
+		/* BCM53573 erratum: 128-byte bursts corrupt frames under load
+		 * (cf. archer-c1200-v2-openwrt patches-6.12/323-*) */
+		ctl |= BGMAC_DMA_TX_BL_64 << BGMAC_DMA_TX_BL_SHIFT;
 
 		ctl &= ~BGMAC_DMA_TX_MR_MASK;
 		ctl |= BGMAC_DMA_TX_MR_2 << BGMAC_DMA_TX_MR_SHIFT;
